      "message": "fix(verify): the mid-turn sweep reads the whole turn, not five poses\n\nLaw (c3) sampled the band stack's column at 4 path stations x 5 turn\nfractions; between them a band could cross stock unseen. It now builds\nswept cells per band (verify/turn_cells.rs): the hull of law (c)'s\ncolumn at a turn interval's two end poses, grown by a proven sag (at\nmost 0.001 mm until the 64-cell cap), swept exactly along each tip\nchord, with the flutes' kerf excused only where the tip stands. The\noverhang backstop keeps its sampled grid (#1316).\n\nPinned by sim midturn_swept_band (clean on main, SweepHit here) and the\nbrute-force probe verify::turn_cells::tests (5 million band positions,\nnone outside the cells).\n\nFixes #1313\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
