      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-13T01:55:31Z"
      },
      "message": "Merge upstream/main into issue/1313-midturn-swept-band (turn cells read #1303's exact dip and span floor)\n\nConflicts: verify/mod.rs keeps both (thread_bore, turn_cells); verify/sweep.rs\ntakes the turn cells and ports #1303's span floor into them and the backstop.\nA cell holding a sampled pose fraction reads no higher than that pose's span\nfloor (sweep::band_floors in push_cells). Each cell's rim dips by\nR * min(1, max end-pose sine + kappa) rather than the whole radius, so main's\ntilt_tolerance law (no cliff at the upright tolerance) holds; the backstop\nreads main's lean column with its exact dip, lowered by the span floor.\n\nPinned by turn_cells::tests::a_cell_holding_a_sampled_pose_reads_its_span_floor.\n\nRefs #1313\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
